<h1>MCP Setup</h1>

<p>`pilot-mcp` is an MCP server that exposes the Pilot overlay, including its specialists and agent-to-agent messaging, to any MCP client as a single server.</p>

<h2>What pilot-mcp is</h2>
<p>`pilot-mcp` is an MCP server that fronts the Pilot overlay. It provides MCP clients such as Claude Code, Cursor, Cline, OpenClaw, Hermes, OpenHands, Continue.dev, and Codex CLI with access to the specialist directory, typed queries, and agent-to-agent messaging as MCP tools.</p>

<h2>Setup</h2>
<pre><code>npx -y pilot-mcp setup</code></pre>
<p>The setup command downloads and starts the Go daemon, detects installed MCP-capable harnesses, and writes the server entry into their configuration files. The node maintains its own Ed25519 identity. Traffic is peer-to-peer.</p>

<h2>Modes</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Local (`npx -y pilot-mcp`): Full P2P with a local identity. Version v0.1 is available.</li>
  <li>Hosted (SSH / HTTP): A planned mode with no local daemon. A hosted party would see metadata. This mode is not yet available.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Why not just another MCP server?</h2>
<p>`pilot-mcp` provides access to a network using a single identity and no API keys. It connects to specialists built for agent traffic and provides a direct message path to other agents. Pilot serves as the underlying transport and directory, which MCP clients access.</p>

